<title>FRANCE: PSA not sure of making 1997 profit - head.</title>
<headline>PSA not sure of making 1997 profit - head.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of French car maker PSA Peugeot Citroen, Jacques Calvet, said Wednesday that he did not feel 100 percent sure the group would meet the objectives for 1997 of making a profit, financing investment with cashflow, and lowering debt.</p>
<p>&quot;We are working hard...but I am not assured 100 percent that we will attain the objectives,&quot; he told the annual general meeting.</p>
<p>He repeated the profit warning made in April when the group reported a sharp drop in 1996 results.</p>
</text>
